\par\par \uc2 Technology & Media\par \b \uc2 Walmart\uc2  to Shut Three Technology Hub Sites --- Retail giant orders hundreds to relocate, considers requiring two days in office\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sarah Nassauer \par \uc2 572 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 February 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Walmart Inc\uc2 . plans to close three of its U.S. technology hubs and require hundreds of workers to relocate to keep their jobs, according to a memo reviewed by The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 The retailer will also begin to require all its technology workers to come into the office at least two days a week.\par \par \uc2 The retail behemoth will close offices that house technology staff in Austin, Texas, Carlsbad, Calif., and Portland, Ore., according to a memo to staff last week from \uc2 Suresh Kumar\uc2 , \uc2 Walmart\uc2 's global chief technology officer.\par \par \uc2 Walmart\uc2  will pay for workers in those locations to transfer to other primary offices, such as San Bruno, Calif., or the company's headquarters in Bentonville, Ark. The company hopes to relocate most of the workers, and some will be allowed to become full-time remote workers, a spokeswoman said. Those that leave will be given severance pay, she said.\par \par \uc2 "We've made the decision to focus our tech team's presence within select locations," said the spokeswoman. Rival \uc2 Amazon.com Inc\uc2 . and other large technology firms have recently announced plans to cut thousands of jobs.\par \par \uc2 In addition, most of \uc2 Walmart\uc2 's global technology workers will need to be in their assigned office at least two days a week, Mr. Kumar said in the memo. Many workers in Walmart's Bentonville corporate headquarters have been required to work in-person five days a week since last year. The shift is a sign that even for technology companies that earlier in the pandemic embraced remote work, in-person work and central offices will play a role going forward. \uc2 Activision Blizzard Inc\uc2 ., publisher of videogames such as "Call of Duty," on Monday stepped up its in-office policy, notifying some employees that they would need to report to offices three days a week beginning in April.\par \par \uc2 The gaming giant's move follows that of \uc2 Walt Disney Co\uc2 ., which said it will require workers to come to its offices four days a week beginning in March. Other employers, including financial giant Vanguard Group, have pushed employees in recent weeks to adhere to existing hybrid-work schedules, often at three days a week.\par \par \uc2 Last year, Mr. Kumar announced plans to open tech hubs in Atlanta and Toronto and plans to hire thousands more staff to his team, which he said was around 20,000 people globally. Before the closures, the company had 11 tech hubs in the U.S. and six abroad, according to its website.\par \par \uc2 Walmart\uc2  has around 1.7 million U.S. workers, the majority hourly staff in stores and warehouses, and about 600,000 in other staff abroad. It recently announced plans to raise its minimum U.S. store wages, amid a tight job market for hourly workers.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the pandemic, Mr. Kumar told its corporate technology staff that remote work would stick around longer than in other parts of the organization.\par \par \uc2 The group aimed to make "virtual work the new normal for Global Technology," Mr. Kumar said in a \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2  post in the spring of 2020. "We've decided that even as restrictions are lifted and other groups in \uc2 Walmart\uc2  eventually return to their offices, we will take our time, and think about how we can invent the workspace of the future."\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Chip Cutter contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020230214ej2e0001v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
