\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Zoom to Lay Off 15% of Staff While CEO Slashes His Salary --- Videoconferencing company's cuts come as work-from-home trend winds down\b0\par\par\uc2 By Will Feuer \par \uc2 437 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 February 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Zoom Video Communications Inc\uc2 . is laying off 1,300 of its employees, or 15% of its staff, becoming the latest technology company to trim its workforce as it adjusts to more normalized trends after a pandemic-fueled growth spurt.\par \par \uc2 Chief Executive \uc2 Eric Yuan\uc2  said Tuesday he was reducing his salary and forgoing his bonus, joining other corporate leaders across finance and technology to take pay cuts this year.\par \par \uc2 He made just over $300,000 in salary for the fiscal year ended Jan. 31, 2022, and about $13,000 as part of a nonequity bonus plan.\par \par \uc2 Shares of the San Jose, Calif.-based company jumped nearly 10% to $84.66. Over the past 12 months, the stock has fallen more than 40%.\par \par \uc2 Once a pandemic darling, Zoom grew rapidly during the Covid-19 pandemic, when companies and consumers turned to its videoconferencing software to connect with one another. That growth has cooled in recent quarters as companies have called employees back to offices and people returned to in-person activities.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Yuan said the company tripled in size in two years. As of Jan. 31, 2022, the company had nearly 6,800 employees, up from about 2,500 employees at the same time in 2020, according to regulatory filings.\par \par \uc2 "We didn't take as much time as we should have to thoroughly analyze our teams or assess if we were growing sustainably, toward the highest priorities," Mr. Yuan said in a message to employees. "I am accountable for these mistakes."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Yuan said he is reducing his salary for the coming fiscal year by 98% and forgoing his fiscal 2023 corporate bonus. Members of his executive leadership team also will forfeit their bonuses and reduce their base salaries by 20% for the coming fiscal year.\par \par \uc2 The company is slated to report fiscal fourth-quarter results on Feb. 27.\par \par \uc2 Zoom joins a wave of technology companies, including \uc2 Dell Technologies Inc\uc2 ., \uc2 International Business Machines Corp\uc2 . and others, that have moved to trim their staffs amid rising interest rates and a leveling off of pandemic-related growth. Business-software companies also have said customers are paring back spending as they look to reel in costs.\par \par \uc2 Various companies have laid off thousands of employees in a round that was led by large technology companies, including \uc2 Microsoft Corp\uc2 . and \uc2 Amazon.com Inc\uc2 . Large companies from other sectors have made similar moves, with \uc2 FedEx Corp\uc2 ., \uc2 3M Co\uc2 . and \uc2 Dow Inc\uc2 . all announcing layoffs in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020230208ej280001a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
