\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: Amazon Cited Over Safety At Three of Its Warehouses\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sebastian Herrera \par \uc2 322 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 February 2023\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Federal labor authorities cited \uc2 Amazon.com Inc\uc2 . for safety violations at three of its warehouses, adding to previous citations the company has faced in a review of its workplace practices.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Department of Labor's Occupational Safety and Health Administration said Wednesday it issued citations to Amazon following inspections at facilities in Aurora, Colo.; Nampa, Idaho; and Castleton, N.Y.\par \par \uc2 The citations follow three recent citations by the department at Amazon sites in Florida, Illinois and New York for similar safety issues.\par \par \uc2 The agency said it found Amazon exposed workers to a high risk of injuries and muscle-related disorders at the facilities due to the fast pace at which workers must handle packages and long hours required to complete tasks.\par \par \uc2 "Amazon's operating methods are creating hazardous work conditions and processes, leading to serious worker injuries," Assistant Secretary for Occupational Safety and Health Doug Parker said in a statement. Amazon faces a fine of $46,875. The agency said it is continuing its investigation into Amazon warehouse safety.\par \par \uc2 Kelly Nantel, an Amazon spokeswoman, said the company takes the safety and health of its employees seriously and doesn't believe the government's allegations reflect the reality of safety at Amazon sites.\par \par \uc2 The Labor Department has been investigating Amazon warehouses after referrals from the U.S. attorney's office for the Southern District of New York. Aside from the three citations in January, the agency in December cited several Amazon warehouses for failing to adequately report injuries. Amazon said at the time that it remained confident in the number of injuries it had reported.\par \par \uc2 Safety issues at Amazon's warehouse have been a central point of disputes between labor activists and the company.\par \par \uc2 U.S. labor data and studies have shown workers at the company are more likely to get injured than in other similar workplaces.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020230202ej2200029\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
